{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
  "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We\u2019ll hear argument first this morning in Case 08-1371, Christian Legal Society Chapter of the University of California- Hastings v. Martinez."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christian Legal Society Chapter of the University of California-Hastings",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCONNELL: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: If Hastings is correct, a student who does not even believe in the Bible is entitled to demand to lead a Christian Bible study, and if CLS does not promise to allow this, the college will bar them from its forum for speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you just look with me at Joint Stipulation 17, I think it makes this completely clear. That's on page 221 of the Joint Appendix, and it states: \"Both parties agreed that in order to become a registered student organization a student organization's bylaws must provide that its membership is open to all students\" -- that's the all-comers policy -- \"and the organization must agree to abide by\" -- \"abide by the Nondiscrimination Policy.\" That's capital N, capital P, a defined term."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But doesn't -- doesn't the one -- isn't the all-comers policy broader than the nondiscrimination policy, so that if you comply with that you automatically comply with everything in the nondiscrimination clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So is this an exception that you want to talk about as it is applied to religious groups, or are you suggesting that if a group wanted to exclude all black people, all women, all handicapped persons, whatever other form of discrimination a group wants to practice, that a school has to accept that group and recognize it, give it funds, and otherwise lend it space?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCONNELL",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There\u2019s a joint stipulation to that effect, Number 34."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCONNELL",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I -- Justice Sotomayor, I believe what we consistently say is that we have been denied the right to meet on campus. And that is completely true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCONNELL",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CLS has all of its activities entirely open to everyone."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GARRE",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is operative. This -- the all-comers policy is how it's implemented in this context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Council of Education",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's explained in the amicus brief for the American Council of Education, explained in the State Universities amicus brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Association of Jesuit Colleges and Universities",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There\u2019s an amicus brief filed by 13 educational organizations representing thousands of colleges and universities across the country, including the Association of Jesuit Colleges and Universities, saying that this is a not-uncommon and a reasonable policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Teach Bible classes? Right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What\u2019s supposed to happen?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, but what is your opinion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I ask about number 2, the -- the so-called line-drawing problem? Aren't you just letting yourself into even more line-drawing problems?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0017",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Number one, it ensures that all students enjoy equal access to all school-subsidized and school-recognized activities. Number two, it avoids the line-drawing problems that we\u2019ve discussed early this morning and I think are necessarily going to arise and also create strife in small educational communities. Number three, it allows --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As I understood the position, your latest position in your brief, you really don't say you have an all-comers policy. There are certain criteria that can be applied, like interest, knowledge; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0018",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "regardless of their status or belief, that gets the school out of the business of determining whether, number one, people are discriminating on the basis of an essential belief, which is, is the way that Petitioner describes his -- their rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, that -- that -- that's pretty tough. That has no connection to merit. I assume there are groups that think subscribing to their beliefs is evidence of merit, particularly religious groups. So, how can you have a -- a test that allows distinctions based on merit but not -- not beliefs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it's pretextual in the Church of Lukumi Babalu Aye sense, yes. No -- no school can purposely discriminate at a group, no matter what policy it adopts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0013",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what if we think that the policy has not been evenhandedly applied? Can't we decide the case on that basis, and then we could just assume arguendo Justice -- the answer to Justice Stevens' question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is -- was there any proof in this record? I mean, there\u2019s a stipulation for summary judgment. Was there any proof showing that it wasn't evenly applied?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this were an employment case, and when an employee is denied promotion the employee said it's for reason A, and then after litigation begins the employer says, well, no, it really wasn't for reason A, it was for reason B because of a policy that we\u2019ve long had, but there\u2019s never -- there\u2019s no written documentation of this new policy; and then at a later point in the litigation the employer says, well, it wasn't really either for reason A or reason B; it was for reason C -- do you think that summary judgment could be granted in favor of the employer on the issue of pretext?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0002-0019",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is the school's policy. It\u2019s supported by substantial history and sworn deposition testimony."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: In your response to Justice Ginsburg concerning California law, is it your position that California law requires religious groups to admit people who do not believe in their religious beliefs and in fact to conduct services of that group?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: Our position is that the registered student organization program is a program of the university; it\u2019s subsidized by the university; it\u2019s recognized by the university; and that all students should be able to enjoy access to that program."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McConnell",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCONNELL: Well, thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. First, in answer to Justice Stevens' question, we do believe that the Court needs to reach the constitutionality of the all-comers policy as applied to CLS in this case. We brought only an as-applied challenge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Put -- put to a side a moment -- forget the as-applied. Just take a -- a pure all-comers policy. Must we decide the constitutionality of that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "65651932be0a2dc2f50d1ec32dc7b3baf6c105e99e40f71d3a41a2a3e8045929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-65651932be0a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1371",
      "confidence": 0.0,
